      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(a\\) for which \\(g(a) = 0\\) for the function \\(g(x) = 3x - 4\\), we start by substituting \\(a\\) into the function and setting it equal to 0.\n\nGiven:\n\\[ g(x) = 3x - 4 \\]\nWe need to solve:\n\\[ g(a) = 0 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\(a\\) for \\(x\\):\n\\[ g(a) = 3a - 4 \\]\n\nSet \\(g(a)\\) equal to 0:\n\\[ 3a - 4 = 0 \\]\n\nSolve for \\(a\\):\n1. Add 4 to both sides of the equation:\n   \\[ 3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4 \\]\n   \\[ 3a = 4 \\]\n\n2. Divide both sides by 3:\n   \\[ \\frac{3a}{3} = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n   \\[ a = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a\\) that satisfies \\(g(a) = 0\\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}} \\]",
